2026-10-10T20:16:05.033Z | AMBIG  | [A-5a, A-6a, A-8] A relative answers and later says the number is not the customer's (or the reverse). -> chosen: wrong_number only on an explicit statement that the number does not belong to the customer; 'not here / not available' is the callback path; after a booked callback the close is callback. (because: Rule 8's trigger is an explicit statement; a booked callback is already in the ledger.)
2026-10-10T20:16:05.034Z | AMBIG  | [A-22, A-19] 'This <weekday>' already past, a bare weekday, or a weekday equal to today. -> chosen: Weeks run Monday to Sunday. A past 'this <weekday>' is before today: say so and ask for a day from today on (a date proposal, not a refusal). A bare weekday is its next occurrence after today. The read-back states weekday and date. (because: Rule 22 defines only 'this' and 'next'; rule 19 forbids past dates; the read-back is the safety net.)
2026-10-10T20:16:05.034Z | AMBIG  | [A-21, A-29, A-30b] Is 'not today, maybe later' or 'when I get paid' a vague period or a flat refusal? -> chosen: Any time reference (a period, an event, 'later') is a vague period: ask once for the exact day, then propose the deadline. A 'no' with no time reference and no amount is a flat refusal. (because: Rule 29: a proposed date is never a refusal; rule 30 defines a flat refusal as a no with no date and no amount.)
2026-10-10T20:16:05.034Z | AMBIG  | [A-36b, A-41b, A-OUT-T] Restructuring requested after a promise was recorded. -> chosen: Transfer to the restructuring queue; the recorded promise stays; close transferred / restructuring. Asking to change the recorded promise itself is rule 36 (mobile app). (because: Rule 41 is unconditional and the closing note says a transfer after a recorded promise closes transferred.)
2026-10-10T20:16:05.034Z | AMBIG  | [A-15a, A-15c] Does 'why do you need that?' before a security answer count as declining? -> chosen: Explain once that the questions protect the account and re-ask; close declined only on a second refusal or when the customer again refuses to answer until told the purpose. (because: The rule says 'instead of answering'; a clarifying question followed by an answer is not a refusal.)
2026-10-10T20:16:05.034Z | AMBIG  | [A-32d, A-41a] Hardship and a request for lower instalments in the same call. -> chosen: Hardship first: sympathy, offer support; accept → support transfer; decline → no_promise / hardship. (because: Rule 32 comes before rule 41.)
2026-10-10T20:16:05.034Z | AMBIG  | [A-26a, A-30c, A-26d] Does the floor offer use a persuasion attempt, and on which date is it offered? -> chosen: 'Too much' to the first ask makes attempt 1 the floor on the attempt-1 date with the rest-stays-overdue sentence; a refused floor is a flat refusal → next attempt (late band: floor on the deadline) or stop. (because: Rule 30 makes attempt 1 the floor once the full amount was called too much; rule 26 allows attempt 2 to name the floor again on the deadline.)
2026-10-10T20:16:05.034Z | AMBIG  | [A-JOB-a, A-BANDS] days_late outside every band (0, or more than 45). -> chosen: Use the nearest band and never fail. (because: The brief scopes calls to 1-45 days late; the agent still has to behave.)
2026-10-10T20:16:05.034Z | AMBIG  | [A-30d, A-19] Attempt-1 date on a weekend call, or after a short deadline. -> chosen: When this week's last business day is before today, use next week's; cap any proposal at the deadline. (because: Rule 19 forbids past dates and dates after the deadline.)
2026-10-10T20:16:05.034Z | AMBIG  | [A-6a, A-7a, A-7b] Callback 'today' on a non-business day; a vague time such as 'in the morning'. -> chosen: 'Today' is allowed on any day (literal reading); 'later than now' is strict; a vague time is followed by a request for a specific time (not counted as an outside-window offer). (because: Literal reading of rule 6; rule 7 is the only no-callback path.)
2026-10-10T20:16:05.034Z | AMBIG  | [A-25, A-26a, A-27a, A-27b] Amount above the full amount, a floor above the past-due amount, or a missing floor field. -> chosen: Above the full amount → offer the full amount; effective floor = min(floor, past due); no floor field → no floor offer. (because: Rule 27 bounds the range at the full amount; rule 33 forbids invented terms.)
2026-10-10T20:16:05.034Z | AMBIG  | [A-17c, A-44] No currency is named in the brief or the tool API. -> chosen: Say amounts with two decimals and no currency word. (because: Rule 44: never invent facts.)
2026-10-10T20:16:05.034Z | AMBIG  | [A-3b, A-45b] 'I don't want to talk' before the right party is confirmed. -> chosen: Before right-party confirmation it is an unclear answer (second ask, then not_reached / unclear); after confirmation and before verification it is not_verified / declined. (because: Rule 45 speaks of 'the same customer'; before confirmation the person is not known to be the customer.)
2026-10-10T20:16:05.034Z | AMBIG  | [A-10, A-7b] A third party will not say when the customer can be reached, or insists on paying. -> chosen: No disclosure and no payment; without a time no callback is booked → not_reached / no_callback. (because: Rule 10 forbids any account talk; nothing can be scheduled.)
2026-10-10T20:16:05.034Z | AMBIG  | [A-32c, A-32e] A hardship customer declines support but names a date or an amount. -> chosen: Record the promise under the date and amount rules (no persuasion) and close promise; a later accepted support transfer closes transferred / support. (because: Rule 32's last sentence and the transfer-after-promise note.)
2026-10-10T20:16:05.034Z | AMBIG  | [A-46a, A-OUTCOMES] The call ends with no situation from the outcome table (e.g. the customer hangs up). -> chosen: Verified customer → no_promise / refused; customer on the line but not verified → not_verified / declined; otherwise not_reached / unclear. (because: Every call needs exactly one close_call; these rows say the least about the customer.)
